{"image_segmentation": "Image segmentation refers to the process of partitioning an image into multiple segments or regions, each representing different objects or areas of interest. It is a critical step in various computer vision applications, enabling further analysis and understanding of the image content.|Here is another description: Image segmentation is a technique used to partition an image into multiple segments or regions, each corresponding to different objects or areas of interest within the image.|Here is another description: Image segmentation is a critical process in image processing, aimed at dividing an image into meaningful and distinct parts. It is essential for identifying and analyzing specific objects or areas within an image, which can be crucial for various applications including medical imaging, object recognition, and scene understanding."},
