{"bbiou_is_robust_and_consistent": "BBIoU is robust and consistent describes the Balanced Boundary Intersection over Union (BBIoU) metric as being reliable and stable in its performance across various conditions and datasets, without showing significant variation or bias."},
{"bbiou__avoids_biases_such_as__erroneous_penalization_and_sensitivity_to_object_size": "The predicate \"avoids biases such as\" indicates that BBIoU is designed to mitigate certain inherent biases present in other evaluation metrics like traditional IoU. Specifically, it aims to eliminate issues like erroneous penalization and sensitivity to object size, ensuring a more fair and consistent evaluation of segmentation models."},
{"erroneous_penalization_and_sensitivity_to_object_size": "Erroneous penalization and sensitivity to object size are specific biases that can affect the accuracy and reliability of segmentation evaluation metrics. Erroneous penalization refers to the unfair penalization of segmentation results due to minor inaccuracies, while sensitivity to object size means that the metric's output can vary significantly depending on the size of the objects being segmented. BBIoU is designed to avoid these biases, providing a more robust and consistent evaluation."},
