{"medical_image_segmentation": "Medical image segmentation is a process that involves dividing medical images into meaningful segments or regions, each corresponding to different anatomical structures or pathological features. This technique is vital for various clinical applications, including diagnosis, treatment planning, and monitoring disease progression."},
