{"f_measure": "F-measure is a metric used for evaluating the performance of boundary estimation in segmentation tasks. It is designed to provide a direct assessment of how well the boundaries of segmented regions match the actual boundaries.|Here is another description: The F-measure is a metric used for evaluating the performance of segmentation models, particularly in the context of medical image analysis. It aims to provide a balanced assessment of segmentation quality by considering both precision and recall.|Here is another description: The F-measure is a metric used for evaluating the performance of segmentation models, particularly in the context of medical image analysis. It aims to provide a balanced assessment by considering both precision and recall, offering a comprehensive view of the model's effectiveness.|Here is another description: F-measure is a statistical metric that combines precision and recall into a single value, providing a balance between the two. It is commonly used in information retrieval and machine learning to evaluate the performance of classification models."},
