{"trimap_iou": "Trimap IoU is a metric used for evaluating the accuracy of boundary estimation in image segmentation tasks. It is specifically designed to assess how well the estimated boundaries match the true boundaries in an image.|Here is another description: Trimap IoU is a metric used for evaluating the quality of segmentation models, specifically focusing on the intersection over union (IoU) within a defined area around the ground truth contour.|Here is another description: Trimap IoU is a metric used for evaluating segmentation models, specifically calculating the Intersection over Union (IoU) within a narrow band of pixels near the ground truth contour.|Here is another description: Trimap IoU is a metric used for evaluating segmentation models, specifically by calculating the Intersection over Union (IoU) within a narrow band of pixels near the ground truth contour."},
