{"extensive_experimentation_and_domain_specific_considerations": "Extensive experimentation and domain-specific considerations involve a thorough process of testing and evaluation across multiple datasets, along with taking into account the unique characteristics and requirements of each medical imaging domain to set the parameter _b_ effectively."},
{"bbiou_metric__does_not_impose__severe_penalties_in_cases_where_the_prediction_boundary_is_more_than_b_pixels_away_from_the_ground_truth_boundary": "The BBIoU metric does not impose severe penalties in cases where the prediction boundary is more than _b_ pixels away from the ground truth boundary. This characteristic allows the metric to provide a more nuanced evaluation, avoiding overly harsh scores in certain scenarios."},
{"severe_penalties_in_cases_where_the_prediction_boundary_is_more_than_b_pixels_away_from_the_ground_truth_boundary": "Severe penalties in cases where the prediction boundary is more than _b_ pixels away from the ground truth boundary refer to the strict scoring approach that could drastically lower the evaluation score if the model's boundary prediction significantly deviates from the actual boundary. The BBIoU metric avoids this by not imposing such penalties.|Here is another description: Severe penalties in cases where the prediction boundary is more than _b_ pixels away from the ground truth boundary refer to the strict scoring mechanism in BIoU that penalizes significant deviations in boundary prediction, potentially resulting in a score of zero."},
