{"bbiou_metric__may_yield__a_score_of_zero_if_the_prediction_boundary_is_more_than_b_pixels_away_from_the_ground_truth_boundary": "The phrase \"may yield\" indicates a conditional outcome where the BBIoU metric can result in a specific score under certain conditions. In this context, it refers to the possibility of obtaining a particular score when the prediction boundary deviates from the ground truth by a specified number of pixels."},
{"a_score_of_zero_if_the_prediction_boundary_is_more_than_b_pixels_away_from_the_ground_truth_boundary": "A score of zero if the prediction boundary is more than _b_ pixels away from the ground truth boundary signifies a scenario where the BBIoU metric assigns the lowest possible score. This occurs when the predicted boundary of an object in the segmentation task is significantly different from the actual boundary, indicating poor performance in boundary detection."},
