{"iou_if_the_value_of_b_is_sufficiently_large": "IoU, or Intersection over Union, is a common metric used in object detection and segmentation tasks to measure the accuracy of an object\u2019s predicted boundary compared to the ground truth. It calculates the ratio of the overlapping area between the predicted and true boundaries to the area of their union."},
{"bbiou_metric__may_unduly_penalize__the_score_associated_with_boundary_patch_evaluation_if_b_is_set_too_small": "The phrase \"may unduly penalize\" indicates a potential negative impact on the evaluation score when certain conditions are met. In this context, it suggests that setting the parameter _b_ too small can lead to an unfairly low score, thus penalizing the model's performance more than is warranted."},
