{"lowest_scores": "The \"lowest scores\" refer to the consistently lower median values that the BIoU metric exhibits compared to other metrics like IoU and BBIoU across the evaluated datasets. This suggests that BIoU is more sensitive to boundary discrepancies."},
{"iou__does_not_necessarily_reflect__precise_boundary_delineation": "The phrase \"does not necessarily reflect\" indicates that while IoU is a commonly used metric for evaluating segmentation performance, it may not always accurately represent the true quality of boundary delineation in the segmented images."},
{"precise_boundary_delineation": "Precise boundary delineation refers to the accurate identification and definition of the edges or boundaries of objects within an image. This is crucial in medical imaging for tasks such as tumor segmentation, where exact boundary detection can significantly impact diagnosis and treatment planning."},
{"biou__emphasizes_on__boundaries": "Emphasizes on indicates a strong focus or priority given by BIoU towards a particular aspect, in this case, the precision of boundaries in image segmentation tasks."},
