{"more_balanced_distribution_and_a_narrower_interquartile_range_iqr": "A more balanced distribution and a narrower interquartile range (IQR) suggest that BBIoU provides consistent performance across different datasets, reducing the variability and biases often seen in other metrics like IoU and BIoU."},
{"bbiou__offers__more_consistent_performance_accounting_for_both_boundary_and_inner_region_accuracy": "The predicate \"offers\" indicates that BBIoU provides a certain type of performance or advantage over other metrics like IoU and BIoU in the context of evaluating model accuracy in medical imaging."},
{"more_consistent_performance_accounting_for_both_boundary_and_inner_region_accuracy": "More consistent performance accounting for both boundary and inner region accuracy refers to BBIoU's ability to provide a balanced and stable evaluation metric that considers both the precision of boundary delineation and the accuracy within the inner regions of the objects being segmented, thus offering a comprehensive assessment compared to IoU and BIoU."},
{"mean_iou": "Mean IoU is a metric used to evaluate the performance of models in medical imaging datasets by measuring the overlap between predicted and actual regions of interest. It is calculated as the average of IoU values across multiple instances within a dataset.|Here is another description: Mean IoU is a metric used to evaluate the performance of segmentation models in medical imaging datasets, representing the average Intersection over Union across multiple instances."},
