{"mean_f_measure": "The Mean F-measure is a statistical metric used to evaluate the performance of models, particularly in the context of medical imaging datasets. It is calculated as the average F-measure across multiple datasets, providing an overall indication of how well a model balances precision and recall.|Here is another description: The Mean F-measure is a statistical metric used to evaluate the performance of models, particularly in the context of medical imaging datasets. It represents the average F-measure across multiple datasets, providing an overall indication of how well a model performs in terms of balancing precision and recall."},
