{"location_dependent_bias": "Location-dependent bias refers to a characteristic where the performance or output of a metric, in this case, BIoU, varies significantly based on the spatial location of the predicted segmentation relative to the ground truth. This bias affects the consistency and reliability of the metric across different locations."},
{"iou__favored__larger_objects": "The term 'favored' in this context indicates a bias or preference shown by the IoU metric towards certain types of objects during evaluation. Specifically, it suggests that IoU tends to give better scores or show higher performance when evaluating larger objects compared to smaller ones."},
{"larger_objects": "Larger objects in this context refer to objects that occupy a greater area within an image, as defined by their bounding boxes. These objects are favored by the IoU metric, meaning that the metric tends to yield higher scores for these objects, potentially leading to a performance gap in evaluations where object size varies."},
