{"the_effects_of_prediction_shifts_on_iou_biou_and_bbiou": "The effects of prediction shifts on IoU, BIoU, and BBIoU refer to the changes in these metrics when a prediction is shifted relative to the ground truth. In the context provided, these effects are demonstrated through a hypothetical example where the ground truth is uplifted by varying amounts, showing how each metric responds to these shifts."},
{"ground_truth__is_uplifted_by__0_to_135_pixels": "The phrase \"is uplifted by\" describes a transformation applied to the ground truth where it is shifted vertically upwards by a specified number of pixels, simulating a prediction error or shift in the object's location."},
