{"issue_of_boundary_misalignment_and_holes": "The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where the boundaries do not align perfectly with the actual boundaries, and there are gaps or holes within the predicted areas. This issue is highlighted by a significant drop in BIoU scores despite relatively high IoU scores.|Here is another description: The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where the boundaries do not align perfectly with the actual object boundaries, and there are gaps or \"holes\" within the predicted areas. This issue is highlighted by the difference between IoU and BIoU scores, where high IoU scores may mask significant problems in the boundary alignment and integrity of the predicted masks.|Here is another description: The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where the boundaries do not align perfectly with the actual object boundaries, and there are gaps or \"holes\" within the predicted areas. This issue is significant because it can lead to lower BIoU scores despite high IoU scores, indicating limitations in using IoU alone for evaluation."},
