{"what_s_outside_the_intersection_fine_grained_error_analysis_for_semantic_segmentation_beyond_iou": "\"What's Outside the Intersection? Fine-Grained Error Analysis for Semantic Segmentation Beyond IoU\" is a research paper presented at the IEEE/CVF Winter Conference on Applications of Computer Vision in 2024, focusing on advanced methods for error analysis in semantic segmentation tasks.|Here is another description: The subject is a research paper titled \"What's Outside the Intersection? Fine-Grained Error Analysis for Semantic Segmentation Beyond IoU.\" This paper likely discusses advanced methods for evaluating semantic segmentation models, focusing on error analysis beyond traditional metrics like the Intersection over Union (IoU).|Here is another description: The subject is a research paper titled \"What's Outside the Intersection? Fine-Grained Error Analysis for Semantic Segmentation Beyond IoU\". This paper likely discusses advanced techniques and analyses in the field of semantic segmentation, focusing on error analysis beyond traditional metrics like the Intersection over Union (IoU)."},
