{"mask_c": "Mask (c) is one of the synthetic prediction masks illustrated in Figure 1, which is used to demonstrate the differences in evaluation metrics like BIoU and IoU."},
{"mask_c__is_created_by__eroding_the_original_mask_using_a_20_20_kernel": "The phrase \"is created by\" indicates the method or process through which Mask (c) was generated. In this context, it specifies that Mask (c) was produced using a particular technique involving image processing."},
{"eroding_the_original_mask_using_a_20_20_kernel": "Eroding the original mask using a 20 \u00d7 20 kernel refers to a specific image processing technique where the boundaries of the mask are reduced or \"eroded\" by applying a kernel\u2014a small matrix used for blurring, sharpening, embossing, edge detection, and more\u2014with dimensions of 20 \u00d7 20 pixels. This process modifies the mask by shrinking its boundaries."},
