{"set_of_boundary_pixels_within_the_ground_truth_mask": "The set of boundary pixels within the ground truth mask represents the edge regions of the object being segmented. These pixels are critical for assessing the precision of segmentation algorithms, as they help determine how well the algorithm can delineate the object from its surroundings."},
{"prx": "_Prx_ is a notation used to denote the set of boundary pixels within the predicted segmentation mask in the context of image segmentation evaluation metrics."},
{"prx__refers_to__set_of_boundary_pixels_within_the_prediction_mask": "The term'refers to' in this context signifies that _Prx_ is specifically pointing to or identifying the set of boundary pixels within the prediction mask, establishing a clear relationship between the notation and the described set of pixels."},
{"set_of_boundary_pixels_within_the_prediction_mask": "The set of boundary pixels within the prediction mask represents the pixels that form the edge or outline of the segmented object in the predicted segmentation, as opposed to the inner region pixels."},
{"equation_4_3": "Equation 4.3 is a mathematical formulation presented in the context to describe a specific metric used in image segmentation tasks. It builds upon previous equations that define the ground truth and predicted segmentations, as well as their boundary pixels."},
