{"proposed_bbiou_metric": "The proposed BBIoU metric is a novel approach introduced in the context for evaluating the performance of image segmentation algorithms. It takes into account both the boundary and the inner region of the segmented object, providing a more comprehensive assessment compared to traditional metrics."},
{"bbiou_metric__considers__both_the_boundary_and_the_inner_region_of_the_segmented_object": "The BBIoU metric \"considers\" both the boundary and the inner region of the segmented object, meaning it takes into account the accuracy of the segmentation in terms of both the outline and the interior of the object."},
{"both_the_boundary_and_the_inner_region_of_the_segmented_object": "Both the boundary and the inner region of the segmented object refer to the two critical components of segmentation accuracy. The boundary represents the outline or edge of the segmented object, while the inner region denotes the area enclosed within this boundary. Accurate segmentation requires precise delineation of both these components."},
