{"boundary_sensitivity_of_the_metric_to_be_tailored_to_the_structural_characteristics_of_the_dataset": "The boundary sensitivity of the metric being tailored to the structural characteristics of the dataset refers to the ability of BBIoU to adjust its evaluation criteria based on the specific details and structures present in the dataset. This adaptability ensures that the metric can effectively evaluate models across a variety of medical imaging tasks with different precision needs."},
{"smaller_b": "The term \"smaller _b_\" refers to a smaller value of the parameter _b_, which is a critical component in the BBIoU metric used for evaluating the performance of models in segmenting object boundaries in medical imaging tasks. This parameter is empirically set per dataset and is a percentage of the image diagonal."},
