{"fine_details": "\"Fine details\" refers to the intricate and small-scale features within an image that require high precision for accurate segmentation. In the context of medical imaging, capturing these fine details is crucial for effective diagnosis and analysis, as they often contain critical information about the structures being imaged."},
{"larger_b": "The term \"larger _b_\" refers to a higher value of the parameter _b_, which is a critical component in the BBIoU metric used for evaluating model performance in segmenting object boundaries in medical imaging tasks. This parameter is empirically set based on the dataset and is expressed as a percentage of the image diagonal."},
