{"coarser_structures": "\"Coarser structures\" refers to the types of object boundaries that are less detailed and more generalized within the dataset. These structures require a larger _b_ value in the BBIoU metric to ensure that the boundary evaluation is fair and aligned with the performance characteristics observed, allowing the metric to be adaptable to diverse medical imaging tasks with varying precision needs."},
