{"high_iou_score_of_0_94": "A high IoU score of 0.94 represents a significant level of pixel overlap between the predicted mask and the ground truth in the qualitative assessment. This score is part of the evaluation metrics used to analyze the performance of the model predictions."},
{"gt1__had__lower_biou_score_of_0_55": "The predicate \"had\" indicates that GT1 experienced or was characterized by a certain metric value during the qualitative assessment. It signifies the presence or occurrence of a specific measurement or score in the context of the evaluation."},
{"lower_biou_score_of_0_55": "The lower BIoU score of 0.55 indicates that despite achieving a high IoU score, GT1 suffered from boundary misalignment issues, leading to a significantly lower BIoU score. This score reflects the degree of misalignment and the presence of holes in the predicted masks, which are critical factors in evaluating the quality of the predictions."},
