{"issue_of_boundary_misalignment_and_holes": "The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where, despite high IoU scores indicating a large area of pixel overlap, there are significant misalignments at the boundaries and the presence of holes, leading to lower BIoU scores.|Here is another description: The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where the boundaries do not align perfectly with the actual object boundaries, and there are gaps or \"holes\" within the predicted areas. This issue is highlighted by a significant drop in BIoU scores despite relatively high IoU scores.|Here is another description: The issue of boundary misalignment and holes refers to discrepancies in the predicted masks where the boundaries do not align perfectly with the actual boundaries, and there are gaps or holes within the predicted areas, leading to lower BIoU scores despite potentially high IoU scores."},
{"gt6": "GT6 is one of the seven cases (GT1 to GT7) used in a qualitative assessment to compare IoU, BIoU, and BBIoU metrics in model predictions across various datasets."},
