{"mask_r_cnn": "Mask R-CNN is a research paper presented at the IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision in 2017. It introduces a framework for instance segmentation, which is an extension of Faster R-CNN that adds a branch for predicting an object mask on top of each RoI (Region of Interest).|Here is another description: Mask R-CNN is a machine learning model designed for object detection and instance segmentation. It extends the Faster R-CNN framework by adding a branch for predicting segmentation masks on each region of interest.|Here is another description: Mask R-CNN is a machine learning model developed for the task of instance segmentation, which involves identifying and segmenting individual objects within an image. It extends the Faster R-CNN architecture by adding a branch for predicting segmentation masks on each Region of Interest (RoI).|Here is another description: Mask R-CNN is a research paper authored by K. He, G. Gkioxari, P. Doll\u00e1r, and R. Girshick, presented at the IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision in 2017. It introduces an extension to the Faster R-CNN object detection framework, adding a branch for predicting object masks."},
